	"_comment": "Slovenčina (Slovak). Composed shape is Subject + passive participle with elided copula (je/bol), exactly how a Slovak status label reads: 'Súbor zmazaný' not 'Súbor bol zmazaný'. No articles (article.none). Masculine passive participles are authored in the long -ný/-tý form (zmazaný, nájdený, začatý); agreement declares a SINGLE uniform rule from that base — strip 'ý', add 'á' (f) / 'é' (n) — verified against all 19 verbs including the -tý outliers (začatý → začatá/začaté), so no per-verb past_f overrides are needed. The 'gerund' slot carries the verbal-noun progress register real Slovak UIs show (mazanie, vytváranie, čítanie); three verbs (aktualizovať, skontrolovať, nainštalovať) take the Latinate/noun register (aktualizácia, kontrola, inštalácia) instead of the native -(ov)anie deverbative because that is genuinely the form Slovak software shows for those specific actions. 'push' and 'commit' have no inherited Slovak verb; pushnúť/commitnúť are the attested informal developer-register loanwords (same borrowing pattern as this codebase's own de.json 'committen'/'gepusht'), flagged here for honesty rather than presented as neutral standard usage. dieťa → deti is a genuine irregular plural (flagged, same treatment as German Kind → Kinder elsewhere in this repo). NOMINATIVE-only composition, accepted deliberately: real Slovak alternates case after numerals (nominative plural for 2-4, genitive plural for 0/5+) and after prepositions/verbs of the fail-sentence; this engine has no case slot, so 'other' is always the plain nominative plural and the fail-sentence object stays nominative rather than the accusative a native speaker would inflect to.",
